# Shared units for disk and volume I/O. In every session (via `units::systems`), not importable.
# title: Shared units (storage)
# description: The I/O operation and IOPS

# One read or write a disk or volume serves. Its own dimension, not `operation`:
# Numbat shows a value in the one unit defined as exactly its unit, so if `IOPS`
# were `operation/s`, every operation rate (Redis, SQL) would print as IOPS.
# Relate the two with an explicit ratio (`io_per_op = 2 io/operation`).
dimension IoOperation

@name("I/O operation")
@url("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOPS")
@aliases(ios)
unit io: IoOperation

# I/O operations per second, as disks and volumes are rated (`500 kIOPS`)
@name("I/O operations per second")
@url("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOPS")
@metric_prefixes
@aliases(IOPS: short, iops)
unit IOPS: IoOperation / Time = io / second
